      "post_id": "89386",
      "author_handle": "haley875",
      "date_as_displayed": "Posted 8 years 9 months ago",
      "body": "I am a working at home parent. This job has a lots of benefits in it. The most important is that you spend more time with your kids. Working at home allows you to be a part of your children's routines throughout the day. Mothers who left careers to raise children can ease their way back into the workforce by working at home. When you travel to work, you are neither working nor spending time with family. Working at home eliminates this waste of time leaves more time for both. Many who are working at home choose hours early in the morning or after the kids have gone to bed. You can make time for yourself as well as your family with the time saved by working at home. Some parents who are working at home, depending on their jobs and the age of their children, can earn a living with part time or no outside childcare. Determining how much child care and what type of child care you need, then work that into your budget.",
